README.md:166:| [Field Name Aliases in Schema-Once Output: Do They Save Tokens?](articles/field-alias-compression-study.md) | Three-part empirical study showing that field name abbreviations are architecturally redundant when compact tabular (schema-once) format already eliminates key repetition. Aliases save a fixed 5 tokens regardless of payload size, while schema discovery costs 85 tokens per roundtrip: a net loss in 75% of scenarios. |
